WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:03.730
- [Interviewer] All right. Ruby?

00:00:03.730 --> 00:00:04.563
- Mm hmm.

00:00:04.563 --> 00:00:05.560
- [Interviewer] Ruby, where'd you grow up?

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:07.490
Where are you from originally?

00:00:07.490 --> 00:00:09.240
- Here, LA.

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:10.351
- [Interviewer] what part?

00:00:10.351 --> 00:00:11.600
- [Ruby] I was born in East LA.

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:13.210
- [Interviewer] East LA.

00:00:13.210 --> 00:00:14.060
And tell me about your family.

00:00:14.060 --> 00:00:19.060
You had both your parents
when you were young?

00:00:19.670 --> 00:00:21.670
- My mom was there, and my dad was there

00:00:24.582 --> 00:00:29.582
I would say physically he was there,

00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:34.480
but he wasn't there like emotionally

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:37.393
or he was an alcoholic.

00:00:39.570 --> 00:00:41.637
- [Interviewer] How would
you describe your childhood?

00:00:44.610 --> 00:00:45.443
- I would say

00:00:51.110 --> 00:00:52.900
people thought it was a family picture,

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:56.340
like it was good, or it
looked like a good family

00:00:56.340 --> 00:01:00.790
but like I said, my dad was an alcoholic.

00:01:00.790 --> 00:01:03.840
My mom used to struggle with five kids

00:01:05.710 --> 00:01:07.423
to pay rent, to feed us.

00:01:07.423 --> 00:01:10.810
He will get paid on Friday
and he won't come back,

00:01:10.810 --> 00:01:12.510
we won't see him till like Monday.

00:01:14.210 --> 00:01:15.510
Check is gone.

00:01:15.510 --> 00:01:18.810
So, I remember a lot of stuff.

00:01:18.810 --> 00:01:23.593
I was molested in elementary.

00:01:26.150 --> 00:01:26.983
I don't know.

00:01:26.983 --> 00:01:28.310
- [Interviewer] Who did that?

00:01:28.310 --> 00:01:30.497
- My teacher, teacher.
Oh no!

00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:35.663
Middleton Elementary School.

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:38.083
- [Interviewer] What grade were you?

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:42.920
- I believe I was a third grader.

00:01:42.920 --> 00:01:46.575
- [Interviewer] Oh no.

00:01:46.575 --> 00:01:48.225
And how far did you go in school?

00:01:50.600 --> 00:01:51.690
- I didn't go to school.

00:01:51.690 --> 00:01:54.070
I went all the way to high school,

00:01:54.070 --> 00:01:55.913
no junior high, eighth grade,

00:01:57.080 --> 00:02:02.080
but I didn't like school.

00:02:02.470 --> 00:02:04.610
I didn't wanna go to school.

00:02:04.610 --> 00:02:06.110
That was one of the reasons I-

00:02:08.720 --> 00:02:11.170
- [Interviewer] You went
on your own at what age?

00:02:13.993 --> 00:02:15.423
- Went at 15.

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:19.683
- Went to the streets?
- I5.

00:02:20.714 --> 00:02:23.643
Yeah. I guess you can say
I went to the streets.

00:02:29.830 --> 00:02:31.473
Associates.

00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:38.743
Well yeah, you can say
I went to the streets.

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:43.520
I will come home late at such a young age

00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:45.270
like at two o'clock in the morning.

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:49.107
At 15, 13, 14,

00:02:49.107 --> 00:02:51.773
sometimes I won't even
come home for like weeks.

00:02:56.130 --> 00:02:57.663
- [Interviewer] Were
gangs a part of your life?

00:02:58.950 --> 00:02:59.783
- Yes.

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:05.530
- [Interviewer] And when did drugs

00:03:05.530 --> 00:03:07.013
come into the picture for you?

00:03:12.030 --> 00:03:15.350
- I remember taking a
first hit of marijuana,

00:03:15.350 --> 00:03:20.350
I was about 10.

00:03:20.690 --> 00:03:23.300
Excuse me, I would like
to have a sip of water.

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:26.910
10, nine, 10, but (gulps)

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:36.920
heroin and cocaine came a little later,

00:03:38.010 --> 00:03:43.010
like about I will say 18, 19.

00:03:50.600 --> 00:03:52.620
I may look a little rough right now,

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:53.920
I'm just going through it.

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:56.720
I don't know if when the last time I see,

00:03:56.720 --> 00:03:58.023
how long ago was that?

00:03:58.023 --> 00:04:00.240
- [Interviewer] It's probably
been four or five months?

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:03.920
- Yeah, oh, so my mom
passed at that time really.

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:06.923
She passed right after Mother's Day.

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:10.843
- [Interviewer] Yeah.
No, it's been since then.

00:04:14.490 --> 00:04:15.520
Sorry about your mom.

00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:16.353
- Yeah.

00:04:18.240 --> 00:04:19.683
- [Interviewer] Where is your drug today?

00:04:22.698 --> 00:04:24.000
- Excuse me, (cries).

00:04:34.479 --> 00:04:39.479
Thank you (crying).

00:04:57.720 --> 00:04:58.620
Heroin (sniffing).

00:05:06.790 --> 00:05:07.803
Oh shit.

00:05:10.145 --> 00:05:11.510
- [Interviewer] And do you have children?

00:05:11.510 --> 00:05:14.860
- I do, I do.

00:05:14.860 --> 00:05:16.010
And grandkids (sniffs).

00:05:21.310 --> 00:05:22.713
- [Interviewer] Were you
able to raise your kids?

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:28.447
- Not as a mother should, no (sniffs).

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:40.363
I mean, it's not like
they were taken from me,

00:05:41.480 --> 00:05:44.470
however, I was taken from
them with the streets

00:05:44.470 --> 00:05:48.763
and the drugs and everything else.

00:05:50.600 --> 00:05:55.600
But yeah I wasn't a mother to them at all.

00:06:00.579 --> 00:06:02.920
- [Interviewer] And who raised your kids?

00:06:02.920 --> 00:06:03.753
- Excuse me?

00:06:03.753 --> 00:06:05.120
- [Interviewer] Who raised your children?

00:06:05.120 --> 00:06:06.573
- My mother and my father.

00:06:07.470 --> 00:06:09.880
My father is been clean off of alcohol

00:06:12.900 --> 00:06:16.983
for like 30 something years.

00:06:18.320 --> 00:06:22.790
But it's weird because I
mean, he's been through it

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:27.870
but while he judges me a whole lot.

00:06:27.870 --> 00:06:32.283
But I mean I don't know,

00:06:32.283 --> 00:06:33.343
I don't get it.

00:06:37.790 --> 00:06:40.150
- [Interviewer] And today
you're living in Skid Row

00:06:40.150 --> 00:06:41.900
in one of the SROs?

00:06:41.900 --> 00:06:43.333
- Actually, I was lucky,

00:06:46.100 --> 00:06:47.563
but it's not healthy.

00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:50.550
I need to get out of there.

00:06:56.280 --> 00:07:01.143
Yeah, somebody offered me a place to stay.

00:07:05.880 --> 00:07:06.730
It's not healthy.

00:07:10.370 --> 00:07:11.203
- [Interviewer] What kind of ways

00:07:11.203 --> 00:07:13.460
have you supported
yourself through the years?

00:07:18.890 --> 00:07:22.173
- Well, I did a lot of,

00:07:25.690 --> 00:07:29.123
I did prostitution once upon
a time, it wasn't my thing.

00:07:29.990 --> 00:07:32.080
It wasn't something I chose to do,

00:07:32.080 --> 00:07:37.080
but I mean, there's a lot of
things you choose not to do,

00:07:37.210 --> 00:07:39.710
however you do them when
you're on drugs (sniffs).

00:07:42.460 --> 00:07:46.790
That, or I used to go to the stores

00:07:46.790 --> 00:07:49.990
or anywhere I could-

00:07:50.876 --> 00:07:52.074
- [Interviewer] Boosting?

00:07:52.074 --> 00:07:55.157
- Boosting (sniffs).

00:08:01.320 --> 00:08:02.330
- [Interviewer] Looking back at your life,

00:08:02.330 --> 00:08:06.343
what are your biggest regrets?

00:08:17.100 --> 00:08:19.650
- [Ruby] Well for one, (sighs) (sniffs)

00:08:26.060 --> 00:08:27.960
not being a good daughter to my mother

00:08:30.350 --> 00:08:32.000
and a parent to my kids (sniffs).

00:08:45.089 --> 00:08:46.950
- [Interviewer] Do you feel
like you were ever loved?

00:08:46.950 --> 00:08:47.783
- [Ruby] Excuse me?

00:08:47.783 --> 00:08:49.583
- [Interviewer] Do you feel
like you were ever loved?

00:08:57.080 --> 00:08:58.013
- [Ruby] Good question.

00:09:01.120 --> 00:09:03.580
My mother, I could say my mother.

00:09:03.580 --> 00:09:05.393
I felt that love with my mom,

00:09:07.100 --> 00:09:10.193
but my father didn't give me that.

00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:18.630
My brothers, you know I'm on drugs,

00:09:18.630 --> 00:09:22.033
yeah, but I never went
and stole from them or,

00:09:24.180 --> 00:09:26.880
I always did that on my
own by prostituting myself

00:09:26.880 --> 00:09:31.683
or like I said, boosting or whatnot.

00:09:36.580 --> 00:09:37.963
- [Interviewer] Did you ever be in love?

00:09:39.370 --> 00:09:42.953
- Wow, I have, however,

00:09:49.110 --> 00:09:50.483
that was rough.

00:09:51.360 --> 00:09:56.360
'Cause I was in love with
the way that this person

00:09:56.380 --> 00:09:58.330
well treated me, was with me.

00:09:58.330 --> 00:10:00.513
It was, I don't know.

00:10:01.373 --> 00:10:02.860
But it was too good to be true of course,

00:10:02.860 --> 00:10:04.700
'cause he got killed.

00:10:04.700 --> 00:10:06.320
I was pregnant with my daughter

00:10:07.183 --> 00:10:09.083
and she never got to see him (sniffs).

00:10:14.190 --> 00:10:15.023
So.

00:10:19.200 --> 00:10:22.109
It was weird because then I

00:10:22.109 --> 00:10:24.230
wouldn't wanna deal with nobody else,

00:10:24.230 --> 00:10:26.840
but there's one person came by

00:10:26.840 --> 00:10:29.300
and again that person got killed,

00:10:29.300 --> 00:10:31.713
so fuck, what the fuck!

00:10:36.270 --> 00:10:38.263
- [Interviewer] Do you feel
sometimes like you're cursed?

00:10:39.970 --> 00:10:40.803
- Yeah.

00:10:47.475 --> 00:10:49.975
Yeah.

00:10:59.564 --> 00:11:00.397
Yeah.

00:11:00.397 --> 00:11:01.423
- [Interviewer] Tell me about karma?

00:11:06.820 --> 00:11:08.683
- Karma, karma.

00:11:09.953 --> 00:11:12.303
Karma's a motherfucker, yes.

00:11:16.099 --> 00:11:18.887
Yeah, I mean a few things
that I'm going through

00:11:18.887 --> 00:11:21.030
I feel like I should be going through 'em

00:11:21.030 --> 00:11:22.630
because of the things I've done.

00:11:35.640 --> 00:11:36.473
Yeah.

00:11:38.875 --> 00:11:40.792
Karma's a motherfucker.

00:11:44.970 --> 00:11:46.590
- [Interviewer] You wonder if
maybe you're paying a price

00:11:46.590 --> 00:11:51.590
